      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In CIF, the seller is typically required to purchase insurance covering the goods before they leave the country of origin (i.e., Korea). The seller must typically provide the inspection report and proof of insurance policy to the buyer before the goods are loaded onto the vessel. If goods are lost, damaged, or destroyed during transit, the buyer can file a claim with the carrier or insurance provider, but the seller is not responsible for the claim. The buyer's insurance policy will typically need to be available before the goods are cleared through customs.",
